{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/995893-exigent-of-vegeance","id":995893,"title":"Exigent of Vegeance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T18:14:33-07:00","id":995893,"title":"Exigent of Vegeance","content":"I have an idea for a game I&quot;m running to introduce an NPC who has inherited the Exigency of Bright Sanguine Saber, Goddess of Vengeance and Betrayal, created before she changed herself into Grandmother Bright and bouncing around from host to host for millennia. I thought it was an interesting idea and it seems to even fit her motif of the time, what with that line about frequently taking proteges and most often pursuing entities who broke heavens laws it seems to me she might have prayed for and received an exigency before making the deal with an eclipse caste that resulted in her lessened state. Anyways I'm not sure if the exigent will end up being a threat or a ally too my players as that is very much up to them and could go either way but I'm sure I'm gonna need some charms and to figure out her excellencies and such and for that I turn to the community for help. Any advice about charm, thematic or crunch would definitely be helpful as well as ideas as to what power level I should assign since from what I understand exigents can be all over the place. Generally I'm just looking for something to get the creative juices flowing so to speak. Plus a lot of the homebrew here is so much more creative than what I come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12171-kaiyen","name":"Kaiyen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:53:28-07:00","id":995904,"title":"","content":"Bright Sanguine Saber was one of the more powerful gods in the history of Creation, if I remember correctly. What manner of horror would cause even she to request the Exigency? That should inform some of the mechanics of the charms, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So: what evil thinks itself above against vengeance and betrayal? Only the sort of evil that thinks itself above anything. The sort of evil that sits on thrones.<br /> <br /> If I were going for this, I'd go big. Tweak the details of canon a little. Bright Sanguine Saber requested the final exigency of the ancient era to create a Chosen without which the Sidereals could never overthrow the corrupt and decadent rule of the Solar Deliberative. Born entirely of grief and stubborn conviction, its birth was so traumatic that the Sun shuttered the fires of exigency and Bright Sanguine Saber spent millennia of outrage in an instant, becoming Grandmother Bright. This is the truth of why she is oddly accepting of Solar Exalted: everything she held against them, she unleashed into the world to their downfall.<br /> <br /> It still hunts. It does not necessarily always hunt the Solar Exalted, though it delights in the opportunity. It hunts those who have station beyond their virtue. In being built to contest the incomparable, the limits this Exigent has reflect the limits of its prey. I would give it an extremely limited supplementary charmset, good access to Ox-Body, and the most dangerous excellency in the game: Inevitable (Attribute/Ability), which acts as an Excellency with a dicecap following the rules of the highest dicecap opposing the Exalted on the scene. It receives a one mote discount to its cost at the end of every round after Join Battle.<br /> <br /> That's the upper limit I would place on a Chosen like this. If you want to go further, you could have the Exigent of Vengeance and Betrayal suffer from a static Essence rating: it is forever frozen at the Essence rating of the prey that inspired its Exaltation (though it changes if its prey refines their Essence further). In that case, when its prey expires, so does the Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}